// =====================================================================
//  Queries for the ToR incast model  (incast.pm)
// =====================================================================
//
//  Bad event Q : at least THRESH packets dropped at the OUTPUT buffer
//                (receiver-facing incast loss)   ->  odrops >= THRESH
//
//  Each run reaches the absorbing "done" state, where odrops/idrops hold their
//  final values, so  P[ F (done & X) ]  is the probability that X holds at the
//  end of the run. (A run is (MMAX+1) substages per slot for HORIZON slots; set
//  the simulation path length above (MMAX+1)*HORIZON, e.g. 5200 for the ranges
//  used here.)
//
//  The ASSUMPTION A is a RANGE (a box) over the input-traffic parameters
//  M (total senders), WIN (sync window), SLEN (burst length); BUF and THRESH
//  are held fixed. We answer "how probable is Q under A" by evaluating prop (1)
//  over that box of constants. Because P[Q] is monotone (increasing in M and
//  SLEN, decreasing in WIN), the box's WORST case sits at the corner
//  (M_lo, WIN_hi, SLEN_lo): if Q is likely there, it is likely for ALL of A.
//
//  Robust box used in NOTES.md  (P[Q] >= 0.64 everywhere inside):
//      A = (M in [6..12]) & (WIN in [0..48]) & (SLEN in [16..24]),  BUF=32, THRESH=8
//
//  Evaluate the whole box:
//    prism incast.pm incast.props -prop 1 \
//      -const BUF=32,THRESH=8,M=6:2:12,WIN=0:8:48,SLEN=16:4:24 \
//      -sim -simmethod ci -simwidth 1e-3 -simconf 0.01 -simpathlen 5200
//
//  Certify the box by its least-favorable corner alone:
//    prism incast.pm incast.props -prop 1 -const BUF=32,THRESH=8,M=6,WIN=48,SLEN=16 ...
//
//  M is even (= 2 * number of active uplinks); WIN >= 0 is fine.

// (1) probability of receiver-facing incast loss  =  P[Q]
P=? [ F ("done" & odrops>=THRESH) ]

// (2) probability of loss at the input ports (stays ~0 in the regime of interest:
//     every uplink buffer is healthy while the receiver overflows)
P=? [ F ("done" & idrops>=THRESH) ]

// (3) is the bad event likely under the current (point) assumption?
P>=0.5 [ F ("done" & odrops>=THRESH) ]
